SUMMARY:Nature Stories at the Art Museum
DESCRIPTION:*This program is taking place at the North Carolina Museum of Art. We will meet at the Welcome Center.* \nJoin us as we open your eyes to the wonderful world of nature through a family-friendly\, nature-filled story time. We’ll begin by sharing a story near the North Carolina Museum of Art’s Welcome Center at 10:30 AM and will then head to other areas of the Art Museum’s campus as we explore natural themes from each day’s stories in a hands-on\, interactive manner. \nThis is a free program beginning at 10:30 AM. Come dressed for the weather and prepared to take a walk! Most walks will be stroller-friendly. Everyone is welcome at this program\, but it has been specifically designed for kids 7 and younger – Nature Stories books and activities were chosen with this age group in mind. \nThe North Carolina Museum of Art is located at 2110 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, NC 27607. Please contact kiersten.bowser@naturalsciences.org with any questions!
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nature-stories-at-the-art-museum/
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art\, 2110 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, 27607
CATEGORIES:Children,Outdoor Experiences,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Kiersten%20Bowser":MAILTO:kiersten.bowser@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
