SUMMARY:Reptile and Amphibian Adaptations
DESCRIPTION:How do turtles survive underwater without oxygen for days on end? How do snakes climb\, swim\, and slither? What is brumation? In this virtual ecoEXPLORE program we will talk about some of the many fascinating adaptations that reptiles and amphibians have evolved in order to survive extreme environments and to sense and navigate the world around them. \nThis program is aimed at kids in grades K-8 interested in being a part of the ecoEXPLORE collaborative science project\, but all are welcome. \nRegister
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/herp-adaptations/
LOCATION:Virtual\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Children,Citizen Science,ecoEXPLORE,K-12 Students,Teens,Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="ecoEXPLORE%20Team":MAILTO:ecoexplore@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
